The [public GitHerald overview](https://aylith-labs.github.io/githerald/) explains the product boundary. It is a **static information page**, not a hosted account, OAuth connection, generation service, or changelog host. The separate June entry records the source publish feature and keeps its old marketing stills withdrawn. This September study shows the **actual locally run app UI** with a disposable SQLite database and synthetic session.

## A fictional draft, reviewed and published locally

The repository `fixture-studio/newsroom-demo`, two source identities, PR #12, release note, and displayed dates are **hand-authored fictional fixture data**, not observed provider events. The source activity links are unavailable, not verified GitHub references. No GitHub OAuth, GitHub API, LLM generation, customer data, or deployed GitHerald app was exercised. The visible **Publish changelog** action did run against this disposable database and created the row shown on the local public route; the published row was not preseeded. Blog and social copy were still drafts, not posted or scheduled.

